      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "While 19th-century restorations are common, synthetic modern binders are rarely mistaken for old residues. To justify moving forward, we would need a specialist to definitively analyze whether the binder is *original* to the restoration or a modern introduction. Proceeding without ruling out a major anachronism risks future challenges regarding authenticity and value. Perhaps we can list the piece as \"Restored\" while further subsurface analysis is conducted.",
      "source": "target",
